{
    "background_story": "Mckenzie was a free-spirited botanist who spent most of her days exploring the vast deserts of the American Southwest. Her obsession was the rare and exquisite Calandrinia, a flower that bloomed only under the light of the full moon. Mckenzie's colleagues often joked that she had a sixth sense for finding the elusive bloom, and her discoveries had shed new light on the plant's unique characteristics. As she wandered through the arid landscape, Mckenzie felt an deep connection to the land and its secrets. She spent years studying the Calandrinia, learning its habits and habitats, and advocating for its conservation. Her work inspired a new generation of botanists and desert enthusiasts, and her name became synonymous with the mystical flower that bloomed under the desert moon.",
